    <item>
      <headword id="idp112548184">dunaidh</headword>
      <description>favourite expression if something went against you, e.g. “A Mhic na dunaidh.” Also in sense of a person not getting what he had been expecting, e.g. a person who had hoped for a construction contract: “Rinn iad an dunaidh air.”</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp112436512">boiseag</headword>
      <description>a handful as in a handful of flour. Also in the sense of a quick wash: “Chuir mi boiseag orm ’s chaidh mi mach.”</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp3224240">spiachdach</headword>
